{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels."}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests"]}],"metadata":{"title":"Privacy Manifests","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" and lists no tracking domains."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy"},{"type":"text","text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle"},{"type":"text","text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report."}]},{"anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Required-reason APIs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), system boot time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), disk space","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), active keyboards","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and user defaults","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). The modules that come nearest:","type":"text"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Module"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it calls"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why none is a required-reason API"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"swift-system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileDescriptor"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"open"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"read"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resize"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unlink"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"createDirectory"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setAttributes"},{"type":"text","text":" (the file protection class), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contentsOfDirectory"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isExcludedFromBackup"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat"},{"text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"FileManager.fileExists","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data.write(to:options:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileVersionStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProcessInfo.performExpiringActivity","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It reads and writes the version file’s contents, never its attributes.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"sysctlbyname","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"code":"hw.machine","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"hw.model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProcessInfo.operatingSystemVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Bundle.infoDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Locale.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"NWPathMonitor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"identifierForVendor","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"None is on the list; ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.vendorIdentifier()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is declared as collected data below.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker’s record timestamps ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A session’s inactivity is measured between records’ wall-clock timestamps, not from the system’s uptime."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Date.now","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wall-clock time, not boot time."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"type":"text","text":", the default clock of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift runtime’s clock, which isn’t on the list."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GRDB"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GRDB ships a privacy manifest of its own."}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every other module calls nothing near the list. Of the packages Traffluent depends on,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"swift-system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Stat"},{"type":"text","text":" API ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FilePath.stat()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileDescriptor.stat()"},{"type":"text","text":") calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fstat"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lstat"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fstatat"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"statfs"},{"type":"text","text":". Traffluent calls none of it. If your app does, your manifest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declares the file timestamp or disk space reason it needs."}]},{"anchor":"Collected-data","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Collected data"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration below is "},{"code":"NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (Traffluent links nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the user’s identity), "},{"code":"NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and has the one purpose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A module declares a type only when it makes data of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that type itself; it is collected only once your app turns the module on and delivers the records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"off the device."}]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Module"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Data type"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What it makes, once your app turns it on","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Device ID (","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeDeviceID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Enricher.vendorIdentifier()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the platform’s "},{"code":"identifierForVendor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as a "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"VendorIdentifierKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Other Diagnostic Data ("},{"code":"NSPrivacyC